@@ -219,11 +219,11 @@ Settings > General has two sections. The Voice rooms and cameras section (`#set-
 | Frequency band | `.band-track`, `.band-step`, `.band-all`, `.station`, `.station-frekans`, `.station-emblem`, `.frekans-dot`, `.station-meta`, `.needle`, `.frekans-sheet-row` | Station states: `.is-tuned`, `.is-target`, `.is-unread`, `.is-mentioned` and the frequency status `.is-open`, `.is-online`, `.is-offline`, `.is-login`, `.is-unknown`. Needle: `.is-dragging`. |
 | Left column and Stations | `.side-left`, `.info-bottom`, `.radio-slot`, `.facts`, `.hints`, `.hints-pop`, `.dm-section`, `.inbox`, `.inbox-head`, `.rooms-list`, `.room-row`, `.room-row-dm`, `.room-row-avatar`, `.room-row-more`, `.top-rooms` | Row states: `.is-current`, `.is-unread`, for voice `.is-connected`, `.is-joining`, `.is-live`, and `.is-blocked` for a direct conversation. A direct conversation row carries `data-dm-id`, All Direct Messages carries `data-dm-more`. |
 | Conversation column | `.convo`, `.convo-head`, `.convo-title`, `.msg`, `.msg-skeleton`, `.channel-start`, `.typing-line`, `.mention-popover`, `.search-panel`, `.search-quick`, `.search-quick-item` | A message that mentions you gets the `--mention-bg` background and a left line. In the Ctrl+K panel the text rooms and direct conversations whose name matches the query (Rooms and People, at most six) sit above the message results, and the down arrow moves from the search field to the first result. A conversation restored from the cache shows no skeleton. |
-| Unread | `.unread-divider`, `.unread-divider-text`, `.unread-bar`, `.unread-bar-actions`, `.new-below`, `.new-below-button` | The New messages divider (`role="separator"`) is a thin `--danger` line with a label at its right end in front of the first unread message, and the message after the divider always starts a new group. When a conversation opens the divider is scrolled into the top quarter of the visible area. The bar (`#unread-bar`, `role="status"`) above the conversation shows the count, the time of the first unread message and the Jump to Unread and Mark as Read buttons. When a range could not be counted the count is a lower bound and ends with + ("99+ new messages"). The two buttons wrap together, and on phones they form one row of equal width under the text. The pill (`#new-below`) sticks to the bottom of the message stream: it counts messages that arrive while the person is scrolled up (`.has-new`, in the accent color, "1 new message below"), and with no new message it becomes Jump to Bottom when the person is more than two screens up. The pill's live region is off because the message log already reads the new message. The Friends view has no bar and no pill. When the whole page counted at startup is unread and older messages exist, the Stations badge ends with + ("50+"). |
+| Unread | `.unread-divider`, `.unread-divider-text`, `.unread-bar`, `.unread-bar-actions`, `.new-below`, `.new-below-button` | The New messages divider (`role="separator"`) is a thin `--danger` line with a label at its right end in front of the first unread message, and the message after the divider always starts a new group. When a conversation opens the divider is scrolled into the top quarter of the visible area. The bar (`#unread-bar`, `role="status"`) above the conversation shows the count, the time of the first unread message and the Jump to Unread and Mark as Read buttons. When a range could not be counted the count is a lower bound and ends with + ("99+ new messages"). The two buttons wrap together, and on phones they form one row of equal width under the text. The pill (`#new-below`) sticks to the bottom of the message stream: it counts messages that arrive while the person is scrolled up (`.has-new`, in the accent color, "1 new message below"), and with no new message it becomes Jump to Bottom when the person is more than two screens up. The pill's live region is off because the message log already reads the new message. The Friends view has no bar and no pill. When the whole page counted at startup is unread and older messages exist, the Stations badge ends with + ("50+") and the accessible name of the row also gives the lower bound ("at least 50 unread"). |
 | Radio card | `.radio`, `.radio-screen`, `.radio-pick-button`, `.crew-item`, `.crew-badge`, `.crew-avatar.has-camera`, `.cam-video`, `.radio-tools`, `.cams-tool`, `.radio-talk`, `.radio-ptt`, `.radio-vad`, `.radio-cam-bar`, `.radio-cam-live`, `.radio-cam-flip`, `.radio-button` | `.is-speaking` and `.has-camera` on crew items, `aria-pressed` on buttons, `.is-mirrored` on your own video (except a rear camera), `aria-disabled` on Flip Camera while switching. |
 | Profile card | `.profile-card`, `.profile-card-band`, `.profile-card-head`, `.profile-card-body`, `.profile-identity`, `.profile-identity-name`, `.profile-identity-badges`, `.profile-identity-handle` | The avatar overlaps the color band. The display name sits to the right of the avatar, the role badges (the base role and a custom role if there is one) right next to the name, and the @username below the name (`13-profile.js buildProfileIdentity`). If the name is long the badges wrap to the next line, and if the card is narrower than 18rem the name, badges and @username move below the avatar. The two preview cards in Settings and the head of the avatar menu use the same layout. If the person has a cover photo it sits inside the band (`.profile-card-band.has-cover`, `.profile-card-cover`, `object-fit: cover`), and the avatar that overlaps it (`.avatar-wrap`, `position: relative`) comes after the band in the tree, so it is drawn above the cover. In Turquoise the band and the cover keep the arch shape. |
 | Avatar menu | `.avatar-menu` | Status options are `menuitemradio`. The head shows the role badges next to the name and the @username below it. |
-| People | `.member`, `.home-view`, `.home-tab`, `.dm-header`, `.people-card` | The Online sheet, the Friends station, the direct message header. When the header does not fit (`ResizeObserver`, `.dm-header.is-tight`) Voice Call, Video Call, the safety badge and Profile become icons only and keep their accessible names, the other person's name stays at least 6rem wide and the Room info button does not shrink. |
+| People | `.member`, `.home-view`, `.home-tab`, `.dm-header`, `.people-card` | The Online sheet, the Friends station, the direct message header. When the header does not fit (`ResizeObserver`, `.dm-header.is-tight`) Voice Call, Video Call, the safety badge and Profile become icons only and keep their accessible names, the other person's name stays at least 6rem wide (phones have no such limit, so the buttons fit on a 320 pixel screen and the name gets shorter) and the Room info button does not shrink. |
 | Sign in card | `.auth-card`, `.auth-dial`, `.auth-needle` | A card shaped like a radio body. |
 | Screen sharing and camera grid | `.cast-panel`, `.cast-head`, `.cast-chip`, `.cast-video`, `.cast-cams`, `.cam-tile`, `.cast-dock-toggle`, `.top-cast-chip`, `.cast-preset` | `body[data-cast="live"]` while the stage is open, `#cast[data-mode="cams"]` for the grid. |
 | Telsiz DJ | `.dj-card`, `.dj-yt`, `.dj-dock`, `.dj-wave`, `.dj-ctrl`, `.dj-vol`, `.crew-dj` | The YouTube player area (`.dj-yt`) is always at least 200x200 CSS pixels regardless of font size, and nothing is drawn on top of it. While the card is hidden or covered, the player is docked in a corner with the `.dj-dock` bar below it. |
